# Restatement ledger (docs/standards/architecture.md rule 9) for the claim that the
# fleet panel body is one arrangement its states differ inside, never a switch between
# arrangements, owned by the "One chart, in every state" section of the module comment
# in apps/web/src/dashboard/fleet-panel-body.tsx.
#
# Membership is a citation: a carrier cites the owner as `fleet-panel-body.tsx` § One
# chart (the bare basename inside apps/web/src/dashboard/, the repo-relative path
# elsewhere), and the sweep's first arm is that citation. The second arm is the owner's
# own heading, which is the positive control. A site restating the claim without citing it is invisible here and
# is a rule 9 finding for review.
#
# docs/standards/react.md's D3 bullets state the claim in the standard's own words and
# are deliberately not cited from here: a change that falsified them is a proposal to
# amend the standard, not an edit to make in passing (the old ledger's "listed, never
# edited" rule, kept).
owner: apps/web/src/dashboard/fleet-panel-body.tsx
claim: one chart, in every state — the body is one arrangement the states differ inside, never a switch between arrangements
sweep: fleet-panel-body\.tsx. § One chart|One chart, in every state
scope: :!docs/tech-debt.md :!docs/friction-log.md :!docs/review-feedback.md
carrier: apps/web/src/dashboard/FleetPanel.tsx
carrier: apps/web/src/dashboard/FleetPanel.structure.test.tsx
carrier: apps/web/src/dashboard/FleetPanel.test.tsx
carrier: apps/web/src/dashboard/Dashboard.tsx
carrier: apps/web/src/dashboard/Dashboard.test.tsx
carrier: apps/web/src/dashboard/Dashboard.deep-link.test.tsx
carrier: apps/web/src/dashboard/dashboard-test-fixture.tsx
carrier: apps/web/src/map/SitePopoverCard.tsx
carrier: docs/design/dashboard-composition.md
